>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dejnirattisai</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>XN</given-names></name><name><surname>Vasanawathana</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Tangthawornchaikul</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Original antigenic sin and apoptosis in the pathogenesis of dengue hemorrhagic fever.</article-title><source>Nat Med</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>921</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12808447</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003037-Zivna1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zivna</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaughn</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalayanarooj</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Stephens</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>T cell responses to an HLA-B&#x0002a;07-restricted epitope on the dengue NS3 protein correlate with disease severity.</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><volume>168</volume><fpage>5959</fpage><lpage>65</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12023403</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003037-Stephens1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stephens</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Klaythong</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sirikong</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaughn</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>HLA-A and -B allele associations with secondary dengue virus infections correlate with disease severity and the infecting viral serotype in ethnic Thais.</article-title><source>Tissue Antigens</source><volume>60</volume><fpage>309</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12472660</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003037-Johnson1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mendez-Fernandez</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Moyer</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Sloma</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Pirko</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Antigen-specific CD8&#x0002b; T cells mediate a peptide-induced fatal syndrome.</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><volume>174</volume><fpage>6854</fpage><lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15905527</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003037-Rodriguez1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rodriguez</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Oleszak</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Leibowitz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1987</year><article-title>Theiler's murine encephalomyelitis: a model of demyelination and persistence of virus.</article-title><source>Crit Rev Immunol</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>325</fpage><lpage>65</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2827957</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003037-McDole1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McDole</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Pirko</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>The role of CD8&#x0002b